<%# SLA Met card for the SLA Trend tab. It deliberately uses the same @counts current-open %>
<%# population as the Open Tickets cards and compliance donut, so its percentage and ticket count %>
<%# always reconcile with those surfaces. At-risk remains a subset of met and No-SLA is excluded %>
<%# by Sla::DashboardScope. The date controls beside this card affect only Created vs Resolved. %>
<%# %>
<%# Same _summary_card anatomy as the Open Tickets tab's row (icon tile, label, big number, muted %>
<%# caption) so the two tabs share one card design and one type scale. The surface is overridden to %>
<%# white: this card stands alone beside the chart rather than in a row of five, where the tinted %>
<%# fills exist to tell the five states apart at a glance. %>
<%= render 'sla_dashboard/summary_card',
      state: :met, label: sla_card_label(:met_window),
      surface: 'tw-bg-white tw-border-gray-200',
      value: safe_join([
        content_tag(:span, sla_percentage(@counts.met, @counts.total), id: 'sla-met-window-percentage'),
        '%',
        content_tag(:span, safe_join(['(', content_tag(:span, @counts.met, id: 'sla-met-window-value'), ')']),
                    class: 'tw-text-xl tw-font-semibold tw-opacity-80 tw-ml-1')
      ]),
      caption: l(:text_sla_met_in_target, met: @counts.met, total: @counts.total) %>
